      "id": "setup-notes",
      "name": "Setup Notes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        440,
        -490
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "height": 410,
        "width": 1100,
        "content": "## Workflow 03S — Source-aware intelligence — DRAFT\nInactive; enabled=false. Manual run is offline and does not invent a success receipt.\n\nUse the existing engine, not the separate V2.0 project. Deploy the reviewed intake API first. Configure a server-side INTAKE_INTELLIGENCE_MODEL, then verify your existing OpenAI credential. INTAKE_INTELLIGENCE_PAID_ENABLED must be explicitly enabled before the server permits one model call.\n\nBind Header Auth to Prepare, Reserve and Store nodes; bind OpenAI credential only to OpenAI Draft Source Plan. No secrets or model guesses are in this export.\n\nThe server loads actual retained sources by event ID, preserves claim IDs / quotes / locations, validates the narrative and all sentence visual fields, and returns a stored receipt only after a valid draft. Free topics without source evidence require research. A missing, refused or invalid model response stops for review; no automatic paid retry.\n\nThe output is a review-pending intelligence draft, not measured scene timing, approved voice or a publishable render. Read quality/SOURCE_INTELLIGENCE_SETUP.md before binding the actual imported workflow ID in the gateway."
      }
    }
